\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Unsupervised intrinsic dimension discovery and eigenvalue spectra in the 3D HJSW model ($N = 20\,000$).} (a) Eigenvalues $\lambda _1, \lambda _2, \lambda _3$ on the late attractor ($\tau = 2.0\,\mathrm  {fm}/c$), confirming that both transverse modes $\lambda _2, \lambda _3$ are suppressed by orders of magnitude below the tangent mode $\lambda _1$. (b) Double U-curves for $\lambda _2/\lambda _1$ and $\lambda _3/\lambda _1$, showing the stable valley centered around $K_{\mathrm  {opt}} \approx 128$. (c) Continuous Participation Ratio $\langle d_{\mathrm  {PR}}(k) \rangle $ across the three hydrodynamic stages without prior knowledge of dimensionality: pure 3D volume at $\tau = 0.20\,\mathrm  {fm}/c$ ($d \approx 2.84$), 2D sheet collapse at $\tau = 0.40\,\mathrm  {fm}/c$ ($d \approx 2.05$), and asymptotic 1D attractor collapse at $\tau = 2.00\,\mathrm  {fm}/c$ ($d \to 1.00$). (d) Scale sensitivity diagnostic $S(k) \to 0$ consistently identifying the optimal neighborhood window $k \in [64, 256]$ across all stages.}}{13}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:hjsw_multipanel}{{5}{13}{\textbf {Unsupervised intrinsic dimension discovery and eigenvalue spectra in the 3D HJSW model ($N = 20\,000$).} (a) Eigenvalues $\lambda _1, \lambda _2, \lambda _3$ on the late attractor ($\tau = 2.0\,\mathrm {fm}/c$), confirming that both transverse modes $\lambda _2, \lambda _3$ are suppressed by orders of magnitude below the tangent mode $\lambda _1$. (b) Double U-curves for $\lambda _2/\lambda _1$ and $\lambda _3/\lambda _1$, showing the stable valley centered around $K_{\mathrm {opt}} \approx 128$. (c) Continuous Participation Ratio $\langle d_{\mathrm {PR}}(k) \rangle $ across the three hydrodynamic stages without prior knowledge of dimensionality: pure 3D volume at $\tau = 0.20\,\mathrm {fm}/c$ ($d \approx 2.84$), 2D sheet collapse at $\tau = 0.40\,\mathrm {fm}/c$ ($d \approx 2.05$), and asymptotic 1D attractor collapse at $\tau = 2.00\,\mathrm {fm}/c$ ($d \to 1.00$). (d) Scale sensitivity diagnostic $S(k) \to 0$ consistently identifying the optimal neighborhood window $k \in [64, 256]$ across all stages}{figure.caption.8}{}}
